  "verbalization": "S-sulphocysteine is implicated in the regulation of L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that S-sulphocysteine acts as a target for several proteins, including fusion glycoprotein F0 and Cytochrome c4, which in turn target specific compounds that ultimately interact with the L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism where S-sulphocysteine influences the activity of downstream targets, which may modulate the function of L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. The overlapping targets and the presence of multiple intermediates suggest a complex network of interactions, possibly involving metabolic or enzymatic pathways. The integration of these evidence points to a possible role for S-sulphocysteine in modulating the activity of L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain through a series of intermediate molecules, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
